cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this atlas, please cite it as below. It is a commissioned review and
  has not been peer reviewed.
type: software
title: 'Neuromodulation: an atlas of exogenous drives, from coupling to outcome'
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Adamek
    given-names: Daniel
    affiliation: The University of Alabama in Huntsville
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: 'https://github.com/danieladamek/neuromodulation-atlas'
url: 'https://danieladamek.github.io/neuromodulation-atlas/'
abstract: >-
  An interactive, volumed atlas of how exogenous drives (brain and nerve
  stimulation, focused ultrasound, light and drugs) act on the nervous system,
  from coupling to outcome, with a graph lab over every mechanism claim the
  review makes. This release is Volume 0 (Foundations): 16 sections, 263
  references, 300 glossary terms, 18 levelled 101s, nine figures and 458 cited
  claims in a claims-only graph, of which 119 are contested and nine are null
  results. It is a commissioned review by Daniel Adamek, drafted with AI
  assistance under the author's direction. It is not peer reviewed. Its literature sweep closed on 15 September 2026. The app code is
  MIT-licensed; the content (the content pack, the data generated from it, the
  graph exports and the rendered text and figures) is licensed CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - neuromodulation
  - brain stimulation
  - knowledge graph
  - claims graph
  - commissioned review
